```javascript
// Instead of:
const doubled = numbers.map(n => n * 2);

// Use:
const doubled = [];
for (let i = 0; i < numbers.length; i++) {
  doubled.push(numbers[i] * 2);
}
```

Or even more readable:
```javascript
const doubled = [];
for (const num of numbers) {
  doubled.push(num * 2);
}
```

This approach makes the transformation explicit and lets you easily add additional logic or debugging statements if needed. The for-loop version is definitely more accessible for developers who aren't deeply familiar with functional programming patterns.

